# Linear handoff (HARD)

Linear status alone is not proof of completion when work was never pushed. **PM cannot review work that is not committed and pushed.**

## Mandatory sequence (every Linear task)

Do this **automatically** when a Linear issue is finished - **do not wait for the human to ask**:

```text
1. Pick up task     → set Linear **In Progress** (from Backlog/Todo)
2. Implement + run  → relevant tests from setup.md; capture **actual output**
3. Commit + push    → `development` only; title/body links Linear issue
4. Linear comment   → one evidence post (template below) - **before** status change
5. Linear status    → **In Review** (never **Done**)
```

**Order is strict:** never post a handoff or move to **In Review** before commit + push succeed. Never hand off with “uncommitted on development”.

## Status names

- Review queue status: **`In Review`** (Linear MCP `save_issue` state name).
- Comment title uses **`Ready for Review - DY-nn`** so it is clear **Cursor** is asserting completion - not an auto-advance or PM sign-off.
- **Never** set **`Done`** - PM (Joey) moves to Done after checking evidence.

## Sprint pickup

When the human says **“pick up sprint X”**:

1. Find that sprint’s **all** open issues in Linear (by sprint/cycle label or milestone - do not cherry-pick a subset).
2. Work each issue as its own task with the sequence above.
3. **Commit + push + Linear handoff after each individual issue** - not one batch at sprint end.
4. Parallelize freely (`Task` subagents or separate subchats) - each worker still finishes with its own commit/push + handoff.

## Rule

**Never** set a Linear issue to **`Done`**. Applies to **every Feature-track Linear issue**, including micro-S. Direct-track work has no Linear ceremony and **no** mandatory commit/push unless the human asked or a Direct batch cycle closes.

## Required comment (single post)

Post **after** push; then set status **In Review**.

```markdown
## Ready for Review - DY-nn (YYYY-MM-DD)

### Acceptance criteria
- [x] <AC verbatim> - <evidence: file/line, endpoint, or UI path>
- [ ] <AC unmet> - <why / what's left>

### How to verify

**Committed code**
- Branch: `development`
- Commit: `<full SHA>` - `<one-line subject>`
- Linear: https://linear.app/<team>/issue/DY-nn/...

**Tests** (paste output or link - not “tests green”)
```text
<paste relevant command + exit code + summary lines>
```

**UI / dashboard** (required for anything visual)
- Preview URL: <deploy or `make dev` tunnel>
- OR screen recording: <link>
- OR local: `make dev` → numbered steps (last resort)

**API / backend**
```bash
# command
# → expected status + body shape
```

**Data / schema**
- Migration / confirm command + how to check

### Reviewer verdicts
| Subagent | Verdict |
|-|-|
| code-reviewer | PASS / FAIL / N/A |
| security-reviewer | PASS / FAIL / N/A |
| api-reviewer | PASS / FAIL / N/A |
| database-reviewer | PASS / FAIL / N/A |
| frontend-evaluator | PASS / FAIL / N/A |

### Deviations from spec
- <diff vs AC/spec, or **None** - must state explicitly>

### Reference
- Spec: `docs/project/issues/DY-nn/spec.md`
- Feedback: `docs/project/feedback/DY-nn/` (when applicable)
```

## Evidence bar (HARD - insufficient handoffs)

| Required | Insufficient |
|--|--|
| `development` + **full commit SHA** after push | “Uncommitted on development”, local-only diff, or missing SHA |
| **Pasted or linked test run output** | “Tests green”, “all pass”, or no command shown |
| **Preview URL or screen recording** for UI/visual AC | File-path list only; “see component file” without how to run |
| AC checkboxes with **verifiable pointers** | ✅ next to AC text alone |
| Comment posted **before** status → **In Review** | Status jump with no comment or empty comment |

- Mid-issue scope growth → call out under **Deviations** (even if approved).
- Prefer Linear MCP (`save_comment` then `save_issue` status) over chat-only claims.

## Local vs Linear

- Repo feedback files stay the detailed review trail; Linear holds the **PM-checkable summary**.
- Update `roadmap.md` / `generator-state.md` to **In Review** (not Done) when you hand off.
- Changelog + patch bump per [changelog](changelog.mdc) when the Linear issue cycle closes (same commit as the task, or immediately before handoff).
